      "writtenOn": "2016-12-13T03:58:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "a) Consider placing all of these functions inside an anonymous namespace. That way, the compiler might be able to warn us about functions that are defined, but never referenced. (I believe this function falls into that bin.)\n\nb) Alternatively, consider using templates to auto-generate this code. I think the following would work:\n\n  template \u003ctypename\u003e\n  struct ReturnNotSupported;\n\n  template \u003ctypename R, typename... Args\u003e\n  struct ReturnNotSupported\u003cR (*)(Args...)\u003e {\n    R operator()(Args...) { return WIFI_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED; }\n  };\n\n  bool initHalFuncTableWithStubs(wifi_hal_fn* hal_fn) {\n    // ...\n    hal_fn-\u003ewifi_initialize \u003d ReturnNotSupported(decltype(hal_fn-\u003ewifi_initialize)){};\n    hal_fn-\u003ewifi_cleanup \u003d ReturnNotSupported(decltype(hal_fn-\u003ewifi_cleanup_stub)){};\n    // ...\n  }",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 82,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 82,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "f3d4f5e036c558cbf6f86e9c99cd6523576d2e23",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
