      "writtenOn": "2016-12-13T05:02:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "On third thought, the idea in part b wasn\u0027t that far off. I think the following would work:\n\n  template \u003ctypename\u003e\n  struct ReturnErrorNotSupported;\n\n\n  template \u003ctypename R, typename... Args\u003e\n  struct ReturnErrorNotSupported\u003cR(*)(Args...)\u003e {\n    static constexpr R Invoke(Args...) { return WIFI_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED; }\n  };\n\n\n  template \u003ctypename T\u003e\n  T MakeStubFor(const T\u0026 val) {\n    return \u0026ReturnErrorNotSupported\u003cT\u003e::Invoke;\n  }\n\n\n  bool initHalFuncTableWithStubs(wifi_hal_fn* hal_fn) {\n    // ...\n    hal_fn-\u003ewifi_initialize \u003d MakeStubFor(hal_fn-\u003ewifi_initialize);\n    hal_fn-\u003ewifi_cleanup \u003d MakeStubFor(hal_fn-\u003ewifi_cleanup);\n    // ...\n  }",
